    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe new `deduplicateCustomerCode` helper is a clean, additive fit for this controller.\n\n- **Right unit / consistency**: This controller already owns all the owner-creation business helpers that query `this.clinicService.findAllOwners().stream()` (`countOwnersRegisteredOn`, `requireCityHasCapacity`, `countNamesakes`, etc.). The new method follows that exact established idiom rather than inventing a new pattern, so a maintainer of *this* codebase would find it natural. It's placed among its peer helpers and invoked inline in `addOwner` alongside the other `owner.setX(...)` computations.\n- **No duplication**: The collision/append logic is new and not repeated elsewhere; it's a single cohesive responsibility in one method.\n- **Not a catch-all**: The method does one thing (de-dup a code) with a clear name and a thorough Javadoc that matches the documentation style of the surrounding helpers.\n- **Idiomatic**: Stream\u2192`Set` of in-use codes, early return on no collision, then the `do/while` incrementing from 2 \u2014 straightforward and readable, consistent with the spec.\n\nNo structural changes needed.",
